# RouteShield AI — master build prompt

Build a complete, deployable hackathon MVP named RouteShield AI. The theme is AI for Accessibility & Inclusion. We have four people and five to six hours. Implement the application, not a landing-page mockup. Use one Express backend and one React frontend. Do not create microservices, chatbots, multiple agents, or a general maps product.

## Product and scope

Pitch: Community evidence becomes explainable, step-free pedestrian route warnings and alternatives.

Problem: Temporary obstructions can make a familiar pedestrian route unusable for people relying on step-free access. A photograph or informal report alone does not provide location-linked, current, corroborated information or a suitable alternative. RouteShield connects community evidence to explicit verification status and profile-specific route planning.

The MVP runs on a fictional, curated pedestrian network. Display “Fictional demonstration network — not live navigation.” Locations, distances, and accessibility attributes are illustrative. Profiles are GENERAL_WALK and STEP_FREE. STEP_FREE is a planning preference, not a certification of wheelchair safety. Do not infer actual path width, slope, GPS location, image authenticity, or whole-route safety from a photograph.

