## Data model

Use private schema `routeshield`, not exposed through the Supabase Data API. Revoke PUBLIC/anon/authenticated access. Use a restricted backend runtime PostgreSQL role with only required grants. Runtime credentials are not migration credentials. Use parameterized SQL and a small connection pool. Use dashboard-provided connection settings, preferably session pooler for an IPv4-only persistent backend, with verified TLS.

Tables:

1. users: id UUID PK default gen_random_uuid(); email normalized lowercase trimmed text UNIQUE length 3–254; display_name text length 1–80; password_hash text; role text USER/MODERATOR default USER; created_at timestamptz default now(). Signup never accepts role.
2. nodes: id text PK; name text; latitude/longitude double precision with geographic bounds; map_x integer 0–600; map_y integer 0–400.
3. edges: id text PK; from_node/to_node text FK nodes; name text; length_m positive integer; step_free_status YES/NO/UNKNOWN; has_steps boolean default false. Enforce canonical from_node < to_node and UNIQUE(from_node,to_node). Edges are undirected. has_steps implies step_free_status NO.
4. incidents: id UUID PK; edge_id FK edges; created_by FK users; status UNVERIFIED/CONFIRMED_BLOCKED/CLEARED default UNVERIFIED; blocked_general and blocked_step_free booleans default false; disputed and requires_review booleans default false; version positive integer default 1; created_at/updated_at/last_evidence_at timestamptz default now(); confirmed_at/cleared_at/dismissed_at nullable timestamptz; moderation_note nullable text max1000. Enforce status/flag/timestamp consistency: UNVERIFIED has no blocked flags or confirmed/cleared timestamps; CONFIRMED_BLOCKED has at least one blocked flag and confirmed_at; CLEARED has no blocked flags and cleared_at. Dismissal is allowed only while UNVERIFIED. Partial UNIQUE(edge_id) WHERE status <> CLEARED AND dismissed_at IS NULL. Index status, updated_at descending.
5. reports: id UUID PK; incident_id FK incidents; reporter_id FK users; claim BLOCKED/CLEAR/UNCERTAIN; description text max500 default empty; photo_key text UNIQUE; photo_sha256 lowercase 64hex text UNIQUE; content_type image/jpeg or image/png; byte_count positive max5242880; latitude/longitude bounded double precision; location_mode SEGMENT_SELECTION; observed_at timestamptz; received_at timestamptz server default now(); analysis_status PENDING/COMPLETE/FAILED; analysis_model nullable text; analysis_json nullable object JSONB; analysis_error_code nullable text; analysis_attempts smallint 0–3 default0; excluded_from_quorum boolean defaultfalse; exclusion_note nullable max1000. COMPLETE requires model and JSON and no error; PENDING has no JSON/error; FAILED has an error and no JSON. Index incident_id/received_at descending and reporter_id/received_at descending.
6. incident_events: id bigint generated identity PK; incident_id FK; actor_id nullable FK users (null for automatic backend actions); from_status nullable valid status; to_status valid status; reason_code text; metadata object JSONB default{}; created_at defaultnow(). Index incident_id,created_at,id. Runtime role can append events, not update/delete them.

No route-history or notification table. Do not persist passwords, JWTs, or secrets in logs. Use the supplied RouteShield-AI-schema.sql if available; otherwise implement the complete contract above.

