## Build priorities, team and checkpoints

Person1 lead: scaffold, freeze contracts, integrate, early deploy, tests/demo/docs. Person2 frontend: five pages, SVG, accessible text flows. Person3 backend/db: auth, migrations, incident policy, deterministic routes. Person4 AI/integration: model contract, image handling, failure/retry behavior, fixture rehearsal. Keep PRs small; GitHub main must stay deployable.

0–20min: freeze schema/routes/state/profile rules, verify one live Gemini image call, create repo/cloud accounts. 20–60min: vertical slice upload → Gemini → persisted UNVERIFIED incident → UI. At60min this must work locally. 60–120min: first deployed frontend/backend/DB, auth and baseline/blocked graph routing. 120–180min: corroboration, disputes, moderator clearing, actual events and rerouting. 180–240min: integrate all pages and error states, accessibility pass, run policy/route tests. 240–300min: deployed end-to-end verification, fix defects, README/deployment guide, rehearse/record4minvideo. 300–360min: buffer, final fresh-URL verification, submission. If only5h are available, finish the same core by300min and omit optional fixtures/features.

Must ship real upload/inference/persistence, explicit verification, profile-specific routing/explanation, JWT auth, deployed site. Cut live GPS/turn-by-turn maps, road-network imports, all-city coverage, CV width estimation, fake image detection, push/SMS/WhatsApp integrations, speech, translation, reputation scoring, multi-agent framework, notification workers, complex dashboards.

